Why this licence
----------------
S.E.M Technology / Rowow releases its core (membranes, cell and stack
architectures, general methods) under CERN-OHL-S. See:

    https://rowow.net/open-technology-charter/

This repository is a plant flowsheet that uses that core (chlorate
leach, CEM electrowinning aisle, BMED regeneration) plus unit
operations that are not Rowow's (induction pyrolyzer, glass digest,
heat ladder). Licensing the design source under the same CERN-OHL-S
keeps the combined work compatible with SEM Tech: anyone who conveys
a modified flowsheet or a Product built from it must convey the
complete corresponding Source under CERN-OHL-S.

CERN-OHL-P-2.0 would be more permissive. It was not used, because a
permissive wrapper around a strong-reciprocal core lets a later party
close the plant design while still consuming the open membrane work.
If you want the weaker or permissive variant instead, replace this
file and the SPDX identifiers before publication.

This project is not a Rowow product. The CERN-OHL-S grant on Rowow
designs does not grant the Rowow name or logo. Do not imply Rowow
endorsement of a build from these drawings.

Covered Source
--------------
params.py, drawlib.py, every *_pfd.py generator, the README, and the
PNG process-flow drawings they produce. Those drawings are Source
and Product documentation for the hardware.

Conveyance
----------
If you Convey a Product (a cell, stack, pyrolyzer, or plant built
from this Source) you must also Convey the complete corresponding
Source under CERN-OHL-S-2.0, and keep the copyright and licence
notices intact.
